{
  "key": "pr-705",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "fix(state): [skip ci] on factory-data commits — kill the phantom push runs",
    "description": "## Problem (live: run 37202005003, 2026-10-04 12:24)
Every machine-sm state publish/snapshot/history push to the `factory-data` branch spawned an instant-fail `event=push` run — zero jobs, "workflow file issue". Root: that branch carries the pre-#671 unparseable `ai-teammate.yml` blob, and the stale push-event registration (the gh-676 "phantom") keeps firing on every state push. Same family as the 09:11:16 / 09:48:38 intermittent reds.

## Fix
Append `[skip ci]` to all three state-commit messages in `js/factoryState.js` (publish / snapshot / history). GitHub creates no runs for pushes whose commits carry the marker — the phantom dies at the source, no matter how stale the registration is.

## Tests
`dmtools run agents/js/unit-tests/run_factoryState.json` — **53 passed / 0 failed** (no message-string assertions; command shapes unchanged)."
  }
}

